Wait a moment—should ErrorState pass the code? The plan doesn't require displaying a code. ErrorState's code prop is used for troubleshooting. WorkflowsView's error usage: `<ErrorState v-if="workflows.error" :message="workflows.error" @retry="workflows.refresh" />`—code isn't passed. Keep it consistent, don't pass code. The error branch's fixed message already carries the semantics.

```vue
    <ErrorState v-if="error" :message="error" :retryable="errorCode === null" @retry="load" />
    <LoadingSkeleton v-else-if="loading" />
    <EmptyState v-else-if="items.length === 0" title="This template has no run records yet" description="When a workflow is initiated in a conversation, its execution records will be shown here." />

